From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:39:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp-display: let the J604 DCP release its
 DISP vote

#1059 lets the J713 DCP release its retained DISP vote while it has
powered the display domains down (put) and asks first whether it can
(check_release). The J604 PMP already carries the same retained DISP and
AGX votes through apple_pmp_display_board() for prepare, check and get;
serve check_release and put there as well.

The DCP calls them only with appledrm.power_gate_ms set (default 0), so
nothing changes otherwise.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
index d30e677b02..6496faef3f 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp-display.c
@@ -539,7 +539,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_check);
 
 int apple_pmp_j713_display_check_release(struct device *consumer)
 {
-	return apple_pmp_j713_board() ? pmp_power_check(consumer, PMP_POWER_DISP, true) : -ENODEV;
+	return apple_pmp_display_board() ? pmp_power_check(consumer, PMP_POWER_DISP, true) : -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_check_release);
 
@@ -557,7 +557,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_get);
 
 int apple_pmp_j713_display_put(struct device *consumer)
 {
-	return apple_pmp_j713_board() ? pmp_power_put(consumer, PMP_POWER_DISP) : -ENODEV;
+	return apple_pmp_display_board() ? pmp_power_put(consumer, PMP_POWER_DISP) : -ENODEV;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_pmp_j713_display_put);
 
